runtime_loader-tls.patch: Code in libr5servo.so (SpiderMonkey) uses initial-exec thread-local storage (R_X86_64_TPOFF32/TPOFF64), which Haiku's runtime_loader does not relocate. The patch gives each such library a static block next to the thread pointer, copies its template there for every thread (libroot calls init_initial_exec_tls() at thread start), and fixes the races this exposed: the template lock is reset after fork(), a template is copied only after its image is relocated (x86_64), a freed slot is not reused, readers take the lock, and a failed load_container() unregisters the template it registered.
